# from_limbs: the 2-limb number with the limbs (h, l) the program gives, which must be canonical;
# each limb guarded (rule R3; milestone1.md, "Values that enter from the program").
kernel:        make_2_limbs
input:         supplied y = h l
output:        x = x0 x1
value:         y
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       represents x
min_precision: 1
source:        constructors (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeMake.v make_2_limbs_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   x1 = guard(l) does not reach x0; a canonical (h, l) has a non-finite l only when h is not finite, which the IEEE-model statement (represents), not data flow, covers

x0 = guard(h)
x1 = guard(l)
